rive, Salesforce).\n*   **Comparison to TaskFlow:** A potential gap for Monday.com is feature complexity. The extensive customization options can lead to a steeper learning curve, which may be a weakness compared to a potentially more streamlined and intuitive TaskFlow interface designed for specific workflows.\n\n#### 3. Pricing Strategy\n*   **Tiered Model:** Monday.com employs a multi-tiered per-seat pricing model: Basic, Standard, Pro, and Enterprise. List prices start at approximately $8/user/month (billed annually) for the Basic plan, scaling to $16/user/month for the Pro plan.\n*   **Freemium Leverage:** Offers a free plan for up to 2 seats, which serves as a low-friction entry point for small teams to experience the platform.\n*   **Competitive Pressure:** This pricing positions Monday.com as a premium solution. For smaller teams or budget-conscious customers, the annual billing commitment and cost at scale can be a significant barrier. This creates a clear opportunity for TaskFlow to compete on price transparency, more flexible billing cycles, or a more feature-rich entry"
